## 2. CANDIDATE DATA MODEL

### 2.1 Enterprise Candidate Entity

The candidate record represents a **person**, not an application. One person can have many applications across many jobs and many years.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    candidates {
        uuid id PK
        uuid profile_id FK "NULL until candidate registers/is onboarded"
        text full_name "NOT NULL"
        text email "NOT NULL, UNIQUE"
        text phone
        text source "career_portal | referral | linkedin | agency | campus | internal"
        uuid referred_by FK "profiles(id), nullable"
        text current_company
        text current_designation
        decimal current_ctc
        decimal expected_ctc
        integer notice_period_days
        text location
        text linkedin_url
        text resume_url "Latest resume path in storage"
        jsonb parsed_resume_data "Structured: skills, experience, education"
        boolean blacklisted "DEFAULT false"
        text blacklist_reason
        timestamptz gdpr_consent_at
        timestamptz created_at
        timestamptz updated_at
    }
```

### 2.2 What Changes from Current

| Current | Enterprise Target | Rationale |
|---------|------------------|-----------|
| `stage` on candidates | **REMOVED** | Stage is per-application, not per-candidate. A candidate at "Offer" for Job A and "Applied" for Job B must retain both statuses |
| `ats_score` on candidates | **REMOVED** | Score is per-application-per-job. Same resume scores differently against different JDs |
| `recommendation` on candidates | **REMOVED** | Recommendation is per-application |
| `missing_skills` on candidates | **REMOVED** | Skill gap is relative to a specific job's requirements |
| `skills` as JSONB blob | `parsed_resume_data` as structured JSONB | Structured extraction: `{ skills: ["React", "Python"], experience: [{...}], education: [{...}] }` |
| `email` nullable | `email NOT NULL, UNIQUE` | Email is the canonical deduplication key |
| No `profile_id` | `profile_id FK → profiles` | Links candidate to auth user when they register or are onboarded |
| No `source` | `source` with CHECK constraint | Required for recruitment analytics |
| No `referred_by` | `referred_by FK → profiles` | Required for referral tracking |

### 2.3 Candidate Lifecycle States

The candidate **entity** has no status. Status lives on each `application`. The candidate entity persists across all interactions with the company — a talent pool record.

```
Candidate lifecycle (at entity level):
  Created (first application) → Active → Hired (for one job) → Alumni (after exit)
  
Application lifecycle (per job):
  applied → screening → shortlisted → assessment → interview → 
  offer_pending → offer_sent → offer_accepted → onboarding → hired
  (or: rejected | withdrawn | on_hold at any point)
```

