### 4.2 Stage CHECK Constraint — The State Machine

```
VALID STAGES (13):
  applied
  screening         — AI scan in progress
  shortlisted       — AI passed, HR reviewing
  assessment        — Assessment assigned
  interview         — Interview rounds in progress
  offer_pending     — Offer being drafted/approved
  offer_sent        — Offer dispatched to candidate
  offer_accepted    — Candidate accepted
  offer_declined    — Candidate declined
  onboarding        — Pre-joining activities
  hired             — Employee record created
  rejected          — At any point
  withdrawn         — Candidate self-withdrew

VALID TRANSITIONS (enforced by DB trigger):
  applied       → screening, rejected, withdrawn
  screening     → shortlisted, rejected, withdrawn
  shortlisted   → assessment, interview, rejected, withdrawn, on_hold
  assessment    → interview, rejected, withdrawn
  interview     → offer_pending, rejected, withdrawn
  offer_pending → offer_sent, rejected
  offer_sent    → offer_accepted, offer_declined
  offer_accepted→ onboarding
  onboarding    → hired
```

### 4.3 Stage History Table — Audit Trail

```mermaid
erDiagram
    applications ||--o{ application_stage_history : tracks

    application_stage_history {
        uuid id PK
        uuid application_id FK "applications(id) NOT NULL"
        text from_stage
        text to_stage "NOT NULL"
        uuid changed_by FK "profiles(id) NOT NULL"
        text change_reason
        timestamptz changed_at "DEFAULT now()"
        integer time_in_previous_stage_hours "Computed"
    }
```

**Every stage transition inserts a row.** This enables:
- Pipeline velocity: AVG time per stage
- Time-to-hire: first `applied` to `hired`
- Recruiter productivity: transitions per recruiter per day
- Compliance: who moved whom and why

### 4.4 UNIQUE Constraint — Duplicate Prevention

```
UNIQUE (candidate_id, job_posting_id)

This means:
  ✅ Candidate A can apply to Job 1 AND Job 2 (different posting IDs)
  ❌ Candidate A cannot apply to Job 1 twice (same posting ID)
  ✅ Candidate A can re-apply to Job 1 AFTER withdrawal (if application is deleted/archived)
```

### 4.5 What This Replaces

| Current Table | Fate | Data Migration |
|--------------|------|---------------|
| `job_applications` | **ABSORBED** into `applications` | Copy `id, form_id→job_posting_id, candidate_id, answers, resume_url, match_score→ai_score, ai_verdict, status→stage, created_at` |
| `candidate_applications` | **ABSORBED** into `applications` | For records not already in `job_applications`: copy `id, candidate_id, job_form_id→job_posting_id, status→stage, ai_score, created_at` |
| `candidates.stage` | **REMOVED** | No migration — column simply dropped |
| `candidates.ats_score` | **REMOVED** | Data exists on applications now |
| `candidates.recommendation` | **REMOVED** | Captured in `applications.ai_verdict` |

