### 5.2 Security Architecture

```
CLIENT can access:
  ✅ assessments (title, description, time_limit, status)
  ✅ assessment_questions (question_text, options) — via RLS filtered to assigned assessments only
  ✅ assessment_assignments (own assignments only)
  ✅ assessment_submissions (own submissions only)

CLIENT CANNOT access:
  ❌ assessment_answer_keys — RLS: SELECT denied for all except service_role
  ❌ Other candidates' assignments or submissions

GRADING happens in Edge Function (server-side):
  1. Receives assignment_id
  2. Fetches submissions + answer_keys using service_role
  3. Computes score
  4. Updates assignment.score, assignment.passed
  5. Updates applications.stage → 'interview' (if passed) or 'rejected' (if failed)
```

### 5.3 What This Replaces

| Current | Enterprise Target |
|---------|------------------|
| `assessments.questions` (JSONB with answers embedded) | Separate `assessment_questions` + `assessment_answer_keys` tables |
| `assessment_tokens` (conflicting `used` vs `status`) | `assessment_assignments` with standardized `status` CHECK |
| `candidate_assessments` (unclear purpose) | **REMOVED** — absorbed into `assessment_assignments` |
| `assessment_attempts` (1 file reference) | **REMOVED** — absorbed into `assessment_assignments.attempt_number` |
| Proctoring violations in React state only | `proctoring_violations` table |
| No per-question submission tracking | `assessment_submissions` table |

