## 9. RESUME MANAGEMENT ARCHITECTURE

### 9.1 Storage Architecture

```
Storage Bucket: resumes (PRIVATE — not public)

File Path Convention:
  candidates/{candidate_id}/v{version}/{original_filename}
  
Example:
  candidates/abc-123/v1/john_doe_resume.pdf
  candidates/abc-123/v2/john_doe_resume_updated.pdf

Access Method:
  createSignedUrl('resumes', path, { expiresIn: 3600 })
  NOT getPublicUrl() — resumes contain PII
```

### 9.2 Resume Version Tracking

```mermaid
erDiagram
    candidates ||--o{ candidate_resumes : uploads

    candidate_resumes {
        uuid id PK
        uuid candidate_id FK "candidates(id) NOT NULL"
        text storage_path "NOT NULL"
        text original_filename
        integer file_size_bytes
        text mime_type "CHECK: application/pdf|application/vnd.openxmlformats..."
        integer version "NOT NULL"
        boolean is_current "DEFAULT true"
        text parsed_text "Raw extracted text"
        jsonb parsed_data "Structured: { skills, experience, education }"
        uuid parsed_by "Edge function ID or 'manual'"
        timestamptz uploaded_at
        timestamptz parsed_at
    }
```

### 9.3 Upload Validation Rules

| Validation | Client-Side | Server-Side (Storage Policy) |
|-----------|------------|----------------------------|
| File size | Max 10MB | Storage bucket policy: 10MB limit |
| File type | `.pdf`, `.docx`, `.doc` only | MIME type check in edge function |
| Filename sanitization | Strip special characters | Storage path uses UUID, not original name |
| Duplicate prevention | Check if `is_current` version exists | UPSERT disabled — always create new version |
| Malware scan | N/A | Future: integrate with ClamAV via edge function |

### 9.4 Resume Parsing Pipeline

```
Upload Flow:
  1. Client validates file type + size
  2. Client uploads to private bucket via signed upload URL
  3. DB trigger on candidate_resumes INSERT fires
  4. Trigger invokes parse-resume Edge Function
  5. Edge Function:
     a. Downloads file from storage
     b. Extracts text (pdf.js for PDF, mammoth for DOCX) — SERVER-SIDE
     c. Sends text to AI for structured extraction
     d. Updates candidate_resumes.parsed_data with structured JSON
     e. Updates candidates.parsed_resume_data with latest version
  6. Client receives success response
```

