## 10. DUPLICATE PREVENTION STRATEGY

### 10.1 Candidate Deduplication

| Level | Strategy | Implementation |
|-------|---------|---------------|
| **Primary key** | Email address | `UNIQUE(email)` on `candidates` table |
| **Secondary check** | Phone number | Advisory check — same phone suggests duplicate |
| **Fuzzy match** | Name similarity | `pg_trgm` extension for `similarity(a.full_name, b.full_name) > 0.8` |
| **Merge capability** | Admin can merge duplicate candidates | Merge function: reassign all applications to surviving record, delete duplicate |

### 10.2 Application Deduplication

| Level | Strategy | Implementation |
|-------|---------|---------------|
| **Database** | One application per candidate per job | `UNIQUE(candidate_id, job_posting_id)` |
| **UI** | "Already Applied" badge | Frontend checks before showing apply button |
| **Re-application** | Withdraw + reapply | Candidate withdraws → application archived → can create new one |

### 10.3 Assessment Deduplication

| Level | Strategy | Implementation |
|-------|---------|---------------|
| **Database** | One active assignment per application per assessment | `UNIQUE(application_id, assessment_id) WHERE status != 'expired'` |
| **Retake** | `attempt_number` increments | Max attempts controlled by `assessments.max_attempts` |

### 10.4 Resume Deduplication

| Level | Strategy | Implementation |
|-------|---------|---------------|
| **Versioning** | Never overwrite | Each upload creates new version; `is_current` flag rotated |
| **Content hash** | SHA-256 of file content | Prevent exact duplicate uploads (optional, Phase 12 enhancement) |

### 10.5 Employee Deduplication

| Level | Strategy | Implementation |
|-------|---------|---------------|
| **Database** | Email unique across profiles | `UNIQUE(email)` on `profiles` |
| **Employee code** | Sequence-generated | `UNIQUE(employee_code)` — no `EMP-{timestamp}` collisions |
| **Candidate → Employee** | Profile linking | `candidates.profile_id` FK links to new employee `profiles` record |

